        <p>_ AUDITORS' CERTIFICATE. 3, KING STREET, BLACKBURN, FFBRUARY 12TH, 1912. To THE MEMBERS OF THE BLACKBURN PittrAsrrnttoPic FRIENDLY COLLECTING SOCIETY. Ladies and Gentlemen,—We have examined the Accounts of the Society for the year ending Dec. 3ls t 1911, and hereby certify them to be correct, duly vouched, and in accordance with law. In the presence of the President, Secretary, and Trustees of the Society, we have inspected the Mortgage Deeds and other Securities belonging to the Society, and have found them in order. We have also ascertaiaed that the Balance in the Bank is correct. We are, yours faithfully, WM. PORTER, ). Chartered Accountants . R. It. PORTER, J Auditors. Htsmict oMrt : CARLTON HOUSE CHAMBERS, 8' 2 SANKEY STREET, WARRINGTON. AGENTS WANTED. SUPERINTENDENT : JOS. FAIRHURST.</p>
