      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-04-20_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <p>-; ..... P'</p>
        <p>CRICKET NOTES.</p>
        <p>The Warrington Club never opened season with brighter prospects. The young idea has matured splendidly with the result that there is plenty of material on which to work. The careful coaching hes borne good results and what is best of all there is a keeness xhibited at the nets which dencte that all are ready and eager for the fray. Active practice has been indulged in during the week, and Fisher, the new professional speaks, in high terms of the players who have put in appearance. Fisher hails from the old nursery school of Yorkshire County cticket Lascelles Half/and is 31 years of age He has had the advant- age c f coaching by that celbrated trio Hurst, Rhodes and Haigh and at present enjoys their friendship. He has acted as profesional for Lascelles Hall, Kirk- beaten and Br( chin (Scotland). Fisher will perhaps be sten to the hest advantage with the bat for it was with the willow that he did good work for the York- shire, team making many good scores As a bowler he comes with a capital reputation whilst he has posses- sion of a gold medal for his brilliancy in the field. The team generally will be somewhat similar to last year but the captaincy will be in the hands of Mr. W. Richardson, jun., Mr. S. Partridge acting as deputy. At least a couple of new hands will appear, hut the probability is that they will graduate first in the second eleven. The fixtures are as follows :</p>
        <p>FIRST ELEVEN. April. 13</p>
        <p>SECOND ELEVEN.</p>
        <p>21 Newton-le-Willows ...A Newton-10-Willows H 27 Boughton Hall A May. 4 Ashton-under-Lyne H Ashton-under-Lyne A 11 St. Helens Recs A St. Helens.Recs H IS Stockport A Stockport H 25 Winnington Park H Winnington Park ...... 27 (Whit-Alunday) Booth A</p>
        <p>June. 1 Prescot H Presrot A S St. Helens 11 St. Helens A 10 Monday Manchester ...A 15 Manchester if</p>
        <p>22 Cheetbam H Cheetham . 29 St. Helens Rees II St. Helens Reca. A July. 0 Cheetham A Cheetham . . lt 13 Stockport tr Stockport A 20 Ashton-under-Lyne A Ashton-under-Lyne -,t 27 Blackly A Blackly H Aug. 3 Wigan H Wigan A 10 Boughton Hall H 17 St. Helens a. St. Helens ll 21 Wigan A Wigan lt 31 Northern Zingari it Sep. 7 Newton-le-Willows H Newton-le-Willows A</p>
