      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-04-20_WidnesExaminer_art0048" n="art0048">
        <head>ANCIENT ORDER OF FORESTERS.</head>
        <p>ANCIENT ORDER OF FORESTERS.</p>
        <p>Quarterly Meeting.</p>
        <p>The 201st quauterly district meeting of the Warring- ton District was held at the Winmarleigh Cafd,Sankfy- street, on Saturday last the 13th instant. The meeting was a unirive one being the first District meeting attended by members of the Female Court. The D.C.R. Bro. Geo Baines occupied the chair, and S.D.O R. Bro.T Rodrn occupied the vice-chair. The following were District delegates :—Court 8335 C R Sister S Healey, Court 138 P.C.R. Bro. S B Healey, Court 240 P.C.R. Bro. H Emmerson, 430 P.C.R. Bro. E Clayton, P.C.R. Bro. W James, Court 431 P.C.R. H Perdue, Court 461 P.D.C.R. Bro. W Orrett, Court 475 P.D.C.R. Bro. J Grayson,P.D.C.R.Bro. P Peacock district treas.,P.D.C.R. Bro. It Thorniley district sec., supported by S.C.R. Sister Buckley, C.T. Sister B Turner, C.S. Sister A Perdue, Sister R 13aines, Court Trustee P.D.C.R. J Walsh, P.D.C.R. H James, District Trustees P.D.C.R. L Davies, P.D.O R. G Maybury, P.D.C,R. W. Hipkiss, P.D.C.R. J Chrimes, P.C.R.A. Jones, P.C.11. J Jenns and P. 0.11. P Wilding. The quarterly returns and cash account were then gone into, and.the D.C.R. congratu- lated the meeting upon the splendid all-round progress that was being trade throughout the District. The auditors report was then taken, and being satisfactory was adopted. The D.C.R. gave his report of the pro- ceedings at meetings of the Manchester High Court Committee. The election then took place of Delegates to August High Court, to be held at Leicester. This resulted in Bro G W It Baines being unanimously elected. P.D.C.R. Bro J Grayson made an appeal on behalf of a Brother in his Court who was in distress. After hearing the circumstances the meeting voted .£3 for this distressed Brother and recommended that an appeal be sent up to the Executive Council OD his behalf. Bro. Grayson thanked the meeting for their generosity and said he had visited every Court in the district On this distressed Brother's behalf,and in every case his appeal had been most generously responded to. It MD decided that a sub-committee be formed to deal with all matters appertaining to the National Insurance Bill' A committee is also to be formed to make all arrangements for the annual bowling pc-nic. The O.C.R.then formerly closed the meeting in accordance with the ritual of the Order.</p>
      </div>
