        <p>• MARRIAGES. GAWNE—PARKER.—On April IGth, at the 7:3,,110 ilari,7o 0 Wesleyan Church, by the Rev. T. Galland the Rev. John Llunnell, Rev. Edward J. 0%61°01 Leyland to Helen Mary, daughter of Mr;vt'reiagt°, Charles E. Parker, Penketh Lodge, near IPRINCE—HooTos.—On the 18th inst. at St' rtcoe ,16.4 Churcb, Wallasey, by the Rev. Samuel 1,1,1101'1,0 Hope, youngest son of Mr. and Mrs. Jame° °WI Prince, of Warrington, to Dorothy Hildred, daughter of Mr. James Hooton of LiverP°° Heathbank Avenue, Liscard, deshire. ,„gro WARRINGTON.—Printed and Published by Ce_An-b1 &amp; Co. (Warrington), Ltd., at The Rxam'a,,-lishesmo Printing Works, Bearse-street, and Pil'Ottnt-al I them at the same place, and also at 2, Offices, Victoria-road, WIDNES. Sr. HELENS. 3, Market-street. Church-street, Marion= APRIL 20 191..</p>
